From: Konoha port <port@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dma: qcom: reconstruct and validate GPI ring DMA pointers

Event RP MMIO exposes the low 32 bits, while ring bases can be 64-bit
DMA addresses. Subtract the low ring base in u32 arithmetic to recover
the ring offset; reject offsets outside the ring or off element boundaries.
The aligned ring allocation is at most 32 KiB and cannot cross 4 GiB.

Use the validated pointer in event draining, stale-event marking and
pause diagnostics. Validate full transfer pointers and include Q2SPI's
high pointer byte. Preserve DMA masks, event acknowledgements, locking,
native lists and callbacks. Invalid event pointers take the software-error
callback path instead of making a circular walk target unreachable.

Add opt-in ring/first-RP checkpoints. The SPI completion storm and hard
lockup are consistent with this bug; the failed capture did not retain
actual DMA addresses, so hardware attribution requires a new test.

Signed-off-by: Konoha port <port@localhost>
